==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Master of Mind Catcrates''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
An interesting crowd-control specialist, Soractes has a wide array of abilities that do function decently, but don't mesh well together in general. His most notable quality is his very high attack speed, which allows him to easily stun-lock any vulnerable [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] through repeated attacks, buying time for your remaining units to catch up. Despite Soractes' low standing range, he can actually outrange many melee Angels, and his Omni Strike even allows him to reach those who would have outranged him like [[Angelic Sleipnir]] and create an opening. His average health and four knockbacks allow him to reposition from aggressive Angel hordes, potentially overturning a losing battle once he rejoins the fight by virtue of his very high speed. His Conjured spirit rounds up his highlights by dealing a small burst of damage and adding a secondary form of crowd-control, weakening hordes of enemies on hit to make them much more manageable.

Despite his promising strengths, Soractes is far from perfect and has a large number of weaknesses. A 0.7 second attack delay simply isn't enough to compensate for the low 30% chance to freeze Angels for just two seconds, and more often than not it requires additional support from the likes of [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen]] to properly bombard these targets, though Soractes' utility against melee Angels is not to be underestimated, as his DPS can make up for times he won't freeze. The reliance on Omni-Strike is also what makes him fairly inconsistent, as he can still have a hard time hitting ranged Angels that he can counter, or fail to outright maintain the freeze even if he does get a hit, and when that happens he has no means with which to properly defend himself. While Sage Slayer makes him a potent counter to [[Tarsiriel]] and [[Ange Lackey]] (provided he can reach them), it still has limited applications in most of the game. Finally, much like [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Doron]], it is worth mentioning the Conjure mechanic can also take some practice to get the timing right, as it is only available once per cycle. This conjure is also very helpful in keeping your own units and Soractes alive for much longer, giving him a better shot at freezing Angels.

