==Trivia==
*Soractes' name may be a portmanteau of 空 ''sora'' (sky/the air, correlating with his [[Sage of Mind Soractes|enemy form]]'s [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] trait) and ''[[wikipedia:Socrates|Socrates]]'', an ancient Greek philosopher. While Soractes' Japanese name is written in katakana, the kanji 空 can also be read as ''kara'' or ''kū'', meaning emptiness or the void/aether element in ''[[wikipedia:Godai|godai]]'', a set of five elements in Japanese Buddhist philosophy.
**Soractes' Japanese name is also very similar to ''practice'' (possibly referring to how he is only the first  [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] and first major [[Zero Legends]] boss; i.e.,  [[Adherence to Virtue]] is a practice round compared to what comes next):
***ソラクティス ''Sorakutisu'' (Soractis) → プラクティス ''purakutisu'' (practice)
**Continuing with the topic of philosophy, his pose is seemingly based on the famous 20th century sculpture of [[wikipedia:The Thinker|The Thinker]], or on [[commons:File:Statues of Plato (left) and Socrates (right) by Leonidas Drosis at the Academy of Athens.jpg|this statue]] of Socrates in the Academy of Athens.
**In real life, Socrates was known to have had an upturned nose and bulging eyes, yet Soractes ironically has neither.
**Soractes' seemingly empty head may allude to "I know that I know nothing," a famous saying widely attributed to Socrates.
***This saying is directly referenced by Master of Mind Catcrates' Korean description, which states that all he knows about cats is that he knows nothing about them.
**Adherence to Virtue may refer to [[wikipedia:Virtue ethics|virtue ethics]], an ethical theory that has its roots in ancient Greece with Socrates, who believed virtue is equivalent to knowledge.
*The capital (top) of Soractes' column appears to combine all three [[wikipedia:Classical orders|orders]] of ancient Greek architecture: [[wikipedia:Doric order|Doric]], [[wikipedia:Ionic order|Ionic]] and [[wikipedia:Corinthian|Corinthian]].
*He and [[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Daybreaker Izanagi]] were the first units to have the Conjure ability.
*He and [[Talents|Ultra Talented]] [[Nurse Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Joyful Nurse Cat]] are the first units to have the Sage Slayer ability.
*The line, "Recently noticed that 'Nyanko' sounds similar to 'Chanko'," in Master of Mind Catcrates's Japanese description is a reference to the Japanese version of the [[Empire of Cats]] [[Empire of Cats/OPEDJP|opening]], in which the narrator makes the same observation.
*Master of Mind Soractes' preview shown when entering [[Legend Stages]] incorrectly says "Stage Clear Bonus 10" instead of "Stage Clear Bonus 11"; the actual 10th clear bonus is [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ancient Egg: N000]].

